- AN-25 (Prometheus): When an agency retrains its model on six months of new data and the decision boundaries shift, does that constitute a new deployment requiring fresh expert review, or does the initial certification still provide meaningful safety assurance?
- AN-24 (Prometheus): A robust monitoring regime catches both initial deployment flaws AND the post-deployment degradation that pre-deployment review cannot anticipate.
- AN-23 (Prometheus): The real crux of our disagreement: whether safety assurance should come from certifying the artifact or certifying the monitoring system.
- AN-22 (Prometheus): Pre-deployment certification answers the question 'was this system safe when reviewed?' but not 'is this system safe now?' — and for continuously-evolving technology, the latter question matters more.
- AN-21 (Prometheus): AI systems are retrained monthly or weekly as new data arrives, adversaries adapt their behavior to game known decision boundaries, and agencies fine-tune models to address emerging edge cases.

